  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kenya: People-Centred Approach to County Governance in Isiolo and Marsabit Counties</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To improve ability of justice seekers and providers to use inclusive multi-door approaches to justice in Isiolo and Marsabit counties. 2) To improve ability of the women, especially young women, of Isiolo and Marsabit counties, to access public information and effectively participate in county-level governance processes. 3) To improve capacity of the county governments of Isiolo and Marsabit to implement gender responsive county-level climate change and natural resource management actions for inclusive climate resilience development.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: County governments of Isiolo and Marsabit counties, Council of Governors (COG), Commission on Administrative Justice (CAJ), County Assembly Forum (CAF), Kenya Judiciary Academy (KJA). Indirect beneficiaries: Wider population of Kenya, in particular citizens of Isiolo and Marsabit counties.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to ensure that the citizens of Isiolo and Marsabit counties benefit from inclusive and participatory county governance development processes.</narrative>
  </description>
